    "description": "# Future Directions \u2014 Functorial Species \u2192 Tropical Valuation Profiles\n\nFollow-up conjectures arising from `Catalog/Bridges/SpeciesTropicalValuationProfiles.lean`,\nwhich established that the species (Day-convolution) product is a **lax min-plus monoidal\nfunctor** into the tropical semiring `(\u2115\u221e, min, +)`:\n\n    min_{i+j=n} (valProfile p a i + valProfile p b j)  \u2264  valProfile p (a \u22c6 b) n,      (\u2605)\n\nand that the EGF subtracts the factorial (Legendre) profile:\n`v_p(a\u2099/n!) = v_p(a\u2099) \u2212 v_p(n!)`.\n\nThe lower bound (\u2605) is genuinely one-sided; the gap is controlled entirely by the `p`-adic\nvaluations of the binomial coefficients `C(n,i)`. The directions below are precise and\ntestable (each is stated so it can be turned directly into a Lean `theorem ... := by sorry`).\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 1 \u2014 Kummer-exact defect formula for the tropical gap\n\nThe defect in (\u2605) is exactly the Kummer carry count. Define the defect\n`\u03b4 p a b n = valProfile p (binConvNat a b) n \u2212 inf_{i+j=n}(valProfile p a i + valProfile p b j)`.\n\n**Conjecture.** When the infimum in (\u2605) is attained at a *unique* index `i\u2080` with finite\nvaluations, then\n`\u03b4 = emultiplicity p (C(n,i\u2080))`,\ni.e. the gap equals the number of carries when adding `i\u2080` and `n\u2212i\u2080` in base `p`\n(Kummer's theorem). In particular, for `p` larger than `n` the functor (\u2605) is **exact**\n(`\u03b4 = 0`), because all `C(n,i)` are then `p`-adic units.\n\n*Testable corollary (easy first target):* for every prime `p > n`,\n`valProfile p (binConvNat a b) n = inf_{i+j=n}(valProfile p a i + valProfile p b j)`.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 2 \u2014 Tropical idempotent / additivity for the species `E` of sets\n\nThe species of sets `E` has constant counting sequence `a\u2099 = 1`, so `valProfile p E \u2261 0`\n(the tropical multiplicative unit). Its self-convolution is `binConvNat 1 1 = (n \u21a6 2\u207f)`.\n\n**Conjecture.** `valProfile p (E \u22c6 E) n = emultiplicity p (2\u207f)`, which is `n` for `p = 2` and\n`0` for odd `p`. More generally the `k`-fold convolution `E^{\u22c6k}` counts `k\u207f`, giving\n`valProfile p (E^{\u22c6k}) n = n \u00b7 emultiplicity p k`. This identifies the **tropical exponential\nlaw** `valProfile (E^{\u22c6k}) = n \u21a6 n\u00b7v_p(k)` and shows the lax functor (\u2605) is *strict* (an\nequality) on the sub-semiring generated by `E` precisely at primes `p \u2224 k`.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 3 \u2014 Derivative species lower the tropical profile by a bounded shift\n\nThe derivative species `F\u2032` has `F\u2032\u2099 = F_{n+1}` (`Species.derivative`), with EGF the formal\nderivative. On profiles this is the shift `valProfile p F\u2032 n = valProfile p F (n+1)`.\n\n**Conjecture (Leibniz tropical inequality).** For the structural product,\n`valProfile p ((F\u00b7G)\u2032) n \u2265 min(valProfile p (F\u2032\u00b7G) n, valProfile p (F\u00b7G\u2032) n)`,\nthe tropical shadow of the species product rule `(F\u00b7G)\u2032 = F\u2032\u00b7G + F\u00b7G\u2032`\n(`CombinatorialSpecies.binConv_leibniz`). Equality holds whenever the two profiles\n`valProfile p (F\u2032\u00b7G)` and `valProfile p (F\u00b7G\u2032)` differ at index `n` (ultrametric\n\"isosceles triangle\" principle).\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 4 \u2014 Eventual periodicity / linear growth of valuation profiles of P-recursive species\n\nMany natural species are P-recursive (their counting sequences satisfy a linear recurrence\nwith polynomial coefficients): linear orders `n!`, permutations, set partitions, etc.\n\n**Conjecture.** For a fixed prime `p`, the tropical valuation profile `n \u21a6 valProfile p a\u2099`\nof a P-recursive counting sequence is *eventually* governed by a Legendre-type formula: there\nexist constants `c, d \u2208 \u211a` with `valProfile p a\u2099 = \u230ac\u00b7n\u230b + O(log_p n)` as `n \u2192 \u221e`. For the\nspecies of linear orders this is exactly de Polignac's formula\n`v_p(n!) = (n \u2212 s_p(n))/(p \u2212 1)`, so `c = 1/(p\u22121)` and the `O(log_p n)` term is the\ndigit-sum `s_p(n)/(p\u22121)`. The conjecture asserts this *linear-plus-sublinear* shape persists\nfor all holonomic species.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 5 \u2014 Tropical profiles separate species up to a finite set of primes\n\nThe EGF is a complete invariant (`Species.EGF_inj`): equal EGFs \u21d2 equal counting sequences.\nThe valuation profile is a *coarser* (tropical) invariant.\n\n**Conjecture (finite tropical reconstruction).** Two counting sequences `a, b : \u2115 \u2192 \u2115` with\n`a\u2099, b\u2099 > 0` for all `n` satisfy `a = b` iff `valProfile p a = valProfile p b` for **all**\nprimes `p`. Moreover, restricting to the finitely many primes `p \u2264 N` already determines\n`a\u2099` for all `n \u2264 N` (since `a\u2099 = \u220f_{p \u2264 N} p^{v_p(a\u2099)}` once `a\u2099 \u2264 N!` is known). This would\nmake the family of tropical profiles `{valProfile p}_p` a *complete* invariant, recovering the\nEGF/analytic invariant from purely tropical (min-plus) data \u2014 a tropical-to-analytic\nreconstruction theorem dual to `CategoricalTropicalUltrametric`'s valuation reconstruction.\n",
